    "body": "## Summary\n- allow leaf service categories to drive the job location contract instead of forcing every job through A→B routing\n- require an owned one-time route quote for `POINT_TO_POINT` categories and reject direct single-location payloads\n- require exactly one validated location for `ON_SITE` categories and reject route quotes\n- persist on-site work in the existing PostGIS service/origin point while leaving destination and route snapshot fields empty\n- expose all selectable leaf categories in the create-job UI and switch automatically between route and single-location map pickers\n- keep exact on-site addresses private while public discovery receives only the coarse area label\n- add focused backend regression tests for both fulfillment modes\n- document fulfillment-specific location/privacy rules\n\n## Architecture / privacy\nNo Flyway migration is required: `jobs.location` already represents the physical origin/service point and destination/route fields are nullable. The backend resolves `fulfillmentMode` from the persisted active leaf category, so the browser cannot downgrade a routed delivery into an arbitrary direct coordinate payload or manufacture a fake A→B route for on-site work.\n\n## Merge gate\nDo not merge unless API verify, web lint/build, container/runtime smoke and payments-ledger smoke are green.",
